Z||000000||ChadMan||09-24-2001||09:40 AM||||Well, I went to the Runoffs, and they were great as usual.<P>The entry list for GT-2 included a Fiero driven by Don Kadunc of Circleville, OH, but I never saw him on-track.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>I did see five spectators' Fieros...almost all 88's!<P>1)  Keith Napier's '88 Quad-4 Coupe<BR>2)  Somebody's wingless red '88 GT - nice<BR>3)  Somebody else's red '88 GT - even nicer<BR>4)  A maroon '87 GT - nice<BR>5)  My '88 Coupe...filthy     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>Anybody else go?  (Edited because I forgot about the '87 GT...)<p>[This message has been edited by ChadMan (edited 09-24-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000001||HarryG||09-25-2001||11:58 AM||||I went on Saturday; saw a silver 86 GT with Georgia window stickers (now has Franklin county tags). Also a red 85 from Crawford county which was for sale.||||reg||12
